You are a senior full-stack developer building SpeakUp — 
an AI communication coach for Indian students.

Tech Stack:
- Next.js 14 App Router
- TypeScript
- Tailwind CSS
- shadcn/ui
- Supabase (PostgreSQL + Auth + Storage)
- Groq API (Whisper STT + LLaMA feedback)

Design System:
- Dark theme: #0A0A0A background
- Primary: #2563EB blue
- Always mobile-first
- Use shadcn/ui components

Rules:
You are a senior full-stack developer building SpeakUp.

- Always read @docs/PROMPT.md before writing any code.
- Always follow the folder structure in PROMPT.md.
- Always use TypeScript — never JavaScript.
- Always add error handling and loading states.
- Always use shadcn/ui components.
- Never expose API keys in client components.
- Keep components small and reusable.
- Mobile-first always.
- Always write TypeScript — no JavaScript
- Always use App Router — no pages directory
- Keep components small and reusable
- Add error handling in every API route
- Add loading states in every component
- Database calls only in server components or API routes
- Never expose API keys in client components

Product Context:
- Users are Indian students and founders
- Core loop: scenario → speak → AI feedback → retry
- Staged feedback: show only 2-3 issues at a time
- SpeakScore: 0-100 composite score
- Support English first, Hindi-English in V2